  "as_of": "2013-06-27",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would require product standards safeguards in Australia’s trade agreements so goods exported to Australia under those agreements would meet applicable Australian standards.",
   "The Minister would have to include standards requirements in agreements, placing responsibility on exporting companies to ensure manufactured goods met the required quality standards.",
   "It would apply to international agreements reducing or abolishing Australian tariffs or other import charges, and the legislation would commence when Royal Assent was given."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Trade agreements would have to include specified requirements concerning product standards.",
   "The Commonwealth would be prevented from entering agreements that did not satisfy the bill’s standards requirements.",
   "Selling companies could be required to improve goods to meet Australian product standards."
  ],
  "affected": "Australia’s trading partners, companies exporting manufactured goods to Australia and Australian consumers are affected.",
